Lemma 4.5. For all i ∈ [k-2], r ∈ [t], u ∈ V, if w ∈ A^r_i is the closest to u in G, then d(u, p_{i+1}(u)) ≤ d(u, A^r_i - {w}) with probability at least 1 - 1/n^2.

P[d(u, p_{i+1}(u)) ≤ d(u, A^r_i - {w})] ≥ 1 - (1 - 1/(2|A^r_i|))^{|A_{i+1}|}

≥ 1 - (1 - 1/(2|A^r_i|))^{(t/4)·n^{1-(i+2)/k}}

≥ 1 - n^{-7}

... by a union bound. Furthermore, $t \cdot k \leq \frac{100}{\log(2)} \cdot n^{1/k} \cdot \log^2 (n) \leq n^3$ for all $n$ sufficiently large ... Hence, $t \cdot k/n^6 \leq 1/n^3 \leq 1/(2n^2)$, so the probability of success is bounded below by $1 - 1/(2n^2)$. By a union bound with Lemma 4.4, $d(u, p_{i+1}(u)) \leq d(u, A_i^r - \{w\})$ occurs with probability at least $1 - 1/n^2$.
